	<key>description</key><string>Send a clipboard image over SSH and copy its remote path or URL.</string>
	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Type `clip` and press Return to upload to your default profile. Use `clip PROFILE` to choose another configured destination. Assign the optional hotkey to upload directly to the default profile.

Use `shot [PROFILE]` to select a screen region and preview the image and destination. Press Return to send or Escape to discard. macOS may ask for Screen Recording permission for Alfred.

Alfred shows the upload status and the copied path or error. Requires the dotfiles `~/.config/scripts/clip-upload`, jq, pngpaste and an SSH profile configured in `~/.zshrc.local`. When remote clipboard support succeeds, Ctrl+V on the server pastes the image.</string>
